{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P21334","secondaryAccessions":["Q7RVL2"],"uniProtkbId":"CRTI_NEUCR","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"1991-05-01","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-06-10","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"1991-05-01","entryVersion":158,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":4.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Neurospora crassa (strain ATCC 24698 / 74-OR23-1A / CBS 708.71 / DSM 1257 / FGSC 987)","taxonId":367110,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Fungi","Dikarya","Ascomycota","Pezizomycotina","Sordariomycetes","Sordariomycetidae","Sordariales","Sordariaceae","Neurospora"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"11017770"}],"value":"Phytoene desaturase"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11017770"}],"value":"1.3.99.-"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2144609"}],"value":"Albino-1 protein"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"11017770"}],"value":"Phytoene desaturase (3,4-didehydrolycopene-forming)"}}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"2144609"}],"value":"al-1"},"orfNames":[{"value":"NCU00552"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11017770"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"18812228"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"2144609"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"11017770"}],"value":"Phytoene desaturase involved in the carotenoid biosynthesis pathway (PubMed:11017770, PubMed:18812228, PubMed:2144609). Converts phytoene into 3,4-didehydrolycopene via the intermediates phytofluene, zeta-carotene, neurosporene and lycopene, by introducing up to five double bonds into phytoene (PubMed:11017770, PubMed:18812228). Is also able to desaturate 1-hydroxyneurosporene into 1-hydroxylycopene and 1-hydroxylycopene into 1-hydroxy-3,4-didehydrolycopene (PubMed:11017770). Gamma-carotene and 1,19-dihydroxylycopene are not accepted as substrates (PubMed:11017770). Neurosporaxanthin is synthesized from geranyl-geranyl pyrophosphate (GGPP) through several enzymatic activities. Phytoene synthase activity performed by the bifunctional enzyme al-2 first produces phytoene from geranyl-geranyl pyrophosphate (GGPP). The phytoene dehydrogenase al-1 then introduces 5 desaturations to lead to 3,4-didehydrolycopene via the intermediates phytofluene, zeta-carotene, neurosporene and lycopene. Al-2 cyclase activity then converts 3,4-didehydrolycopene into torulene. Al-2 can also convet lycopene into gamma-carotene which in turn is converted to beta-carotene by an additional al-2 cyclization reaction. Torulene is the substrate of the dioxidase cao-2 that breaks the molecule, removing five carbon atoms to yield beta-apo-4'-carotenal, whereas the aldehyde dehydrogenase ylo-1 mediates the last step by converting beta-apo-4'-carotenal into neurosporaxanthin (Probable)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"15-cis-phytoene + A = all-trans-phytofluene + AH2","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:30603"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:13193"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:17499"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:27787"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:28129"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11017770"}]},"physiologicalReactions":[{"directionType":"left-to-right","reactionCrossReference":{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:30604"},"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11017770"}]}]},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"all-trans-phytofluene + A = all-trans-zeta-carotene + AH2","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHE